  "claims": [
    {
      "id": "claim_7df45c000b2a4d2da39b79dba43a075c",
      "statement": "A Trusted Action is a named, auditable operation the server runs against a managed cluster or AWS account on a caller's behalf; callers submit it through the API rather than reaching the cluster or account directly, and the server authorizes, provisions a least-privilege session, executes, and audits it.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://docs/adding-a-trusted-action.md#L16-L23",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:f443640e1febce56f9d1f13efb7a6655ca95e32c5fdf059c37ad8acdeea7a12d:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_80ba1b5669204ec285f5825122daaf0a",
      "statement": "The Action interface is scope-independent and has no Execute method; KubeAction and AWSAction are the scope-specific subtypes that add RequiredRBAC/RequiredServices and Execute, so an action can only run through the scope that authorizes it and provisions its clients.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://internal/actions/actions.go#L73-L97",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:e05e42fce1c7ca7e0ff27a1f6778df6e33bd771ef5d7f49bee3e49252fd80c73:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_f24b9ff9eb4b4649974f6b95ffbb01c5",
      "statement": "AWSWriteAction extends AWSAction with Operation() and Resource(); AWSScope derives the write operation to check against the allowlist purely via a type assertion to AWSWriteAction, so an action that mutates AWS state but implements only AWSAction is treated as a read and runs unconditionally without any ROSA_TA_AWS_ALLOWED_OPERATIONS check.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://docs/adding-a-trusted-action.md#L95-L107",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:4d5daa092cbd99ab28a1cb7d8dc73fabe82873f71149dc08ea0af8783d32bd32:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://internal/executor/aws.go#L100-L114",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:e709c293656a146e975bde0973cfdb77a2383fbc6d499519b762eb79fbbdac0b:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_5ce8ffcda6c54bf4b2784b8bd238ac4e",
      "statement": "AWSWriteAction.Resource() fixes the kind of object a write action acts on; AWSScope.DeriveTarget refuses a request whose caller-supplied resource param disagrees with write.Resource() rather than overriding it, preventing a caller from redirecting a write to a different resource kind.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://internal/executor/aws.go#L59-L76",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:9b1baac282fa61ddd75f1667a6dd01468b38ac743a98ac1a68377f8f2fc92865:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_f60f7e4eaf464bddb10df2f24e5f49a7",
      "statement": "Catalog Type: openapi.Write is descriptive metadata only and is never cross-checked against whether the action's Go type actually implements AWSWriteAction, so getting the interface right is solely the implementation's responsibility.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://docs/adding-a-trusted-action.md#L104-L106",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:a388ca0b6ded9b22943247608330f4eb5331d0e32694738e855be8c8739537fa:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_304ba053abb549789e2b6ab17e570ce6",
      "statement": "ActionResult carries Resources ([]map[string]interface{}) and a human-readable Message; resourcesFrom converts Kubernetes unstructured.Unstructured objects directly via their .Object field, while awsResourcesFrom round-trips AWS SDK structs through JSON marshal/unmarshal because they carry no JSON tags.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://internal/actions/actions.go#L157-L187",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:b760cbe0d1ab717b3b784f0f03bb8c642f0fd9358b77641b2a576410db67e5d8:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://internal/actions/actions.go#L68-L71",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:c08dac2683799ffe7a837139f244ecbde61fbfeb78b0fb7df25d1d83999dd3b1:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_46d2d43619624beca4cf393fb6092294",
      "statement": "pruneUnset recursively deletes nil-valued map keys from AWS objects converted by awsResourcesFrom (since a nil SDK pointer means 'absent'), but does not strip nulls from list elements because an element's position can be meaningful.",
      "evidence": [
