    },
    {
      "id": "claim_5472b5df0ad1437495b78c52662782ae",
      "statement": "RegisterActionFactory stores a factory function keyed by the action's Name(), giving each execution a fresh action value; CreateAction looks up and invokes that factory by name, returning nil if no action is registered under that name, which the worker treats as 'unknown action'.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://docs/adding-a-trusted-action.md#L34-L36",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:e0f576df92306d2048dcbe18674df864c4295371b50b3e9a1de8e9e4da42ff83:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://internal/actions/actions.go#L125-L145",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:ca62117242217eb6afa2c30b6d8842193d1f7afeaa49773e7b7b08b6b5b4d032:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_23f4159c09a34e1582a7502e1826e94c",
      "statement": "An action requires two independent, mandatory registrations: the implementation + init() self-registration in internal/actions/<name>.go, and an ActionDefinition in internal/catalog/catalog.go; a catalog entry without an implementation fails at worker execution with 'unknown action', while an implementation without a catalog entry returns 404 from the API handlers before the registry is ever consulted.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://docs/adding-a-trusted-action.md#L24-L39",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:485575966450eb60b731877675813ff59fab4dabdc2928fe5fcbc095f79a4687:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://internal/catalog/catalog.go#L185-L200",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:90f0765b183b1acda53b85b23551188d8cec25049845bbab4be32b0a3a707650:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_6474a715648e4d3f9e04df7a8898dcc1",
      "statement": "ActionDefinition's Params are descriptive only: the API does not reject a request for omitting a Required param at submission time, returning 202 regardless, so each action must validate its own required parameters at Execute time.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://docs/adding-a-trusted-action.md#L201-L207",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:ade272389c12c6bb7f04af5fc87126dac75f8f0adf499ab55fdbf963ce7aa9de:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_11ae94b13e7a4eeab7db7a88cd4e0a43",
      "statement": "aws-reboot and aws-terminate both act exclusively on EC2 instances identified by a fixed Resource() of 'ec2-instances' and call requireClusterInstance before mutating, which refuses to proceed unless the target instance carries the requesting cluster's kubernetes.io/cluster/<infraID>=owned tag, bounding a write action's blast radius to the owning cluster rather than the whole shared AWS account.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://internal/actions/aws_write.go#L19-L94",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:a6e90446db0ebde85286b9c3094f5c30d7e0ff0df20645ec4f4152fb8650544d:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_4374743a64864ae9adf75177b2979437",
      "statement": "aws-terminate is restricted to the SREP role in the catalog, narrower than the allRoles granted to most other actions, because termination is irreversible.",
